WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.500
Ask who owns training and
three offices answer at once.

2
00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:08.225
Between them, nobody owns whether people
can do the new job on the day it changes.

3
00:00:08.225 --> 00:00:10.725
So the program keeps one decider per row.

4
00:00:10.725 --> 00:00:13.252
The sponsor and C I O fund the learning

5
00:00:13.252 --> 00:00:16.350
program and decide each
wave's readiness plan.

6
00:00:16.350 --> 00:00:20.253
The CISO owns the training
policy, the completion threshold,

7
00:00:20.253 --> 00:00:25.150
and the exact words users are taught about
sign-in, reporting and the help desk.

8
00:00:25.150 --> 00:00:29.206
The chief human capital officer's
office owns workforce strategy,

9
00:00:29.206 --> 00:00:33.263
position coding, the facts behind
the rosters, and labor relations.

10
00:00:33.263 --> 00:00:36.900
The training lead builds the
curriculum and reports the numbers,

11
00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:38.651
but never declares a wave ready.

12
00:00:38.651 --> 00:00:41.575
The I S S O reviews the training record.

13
00:00:41.575 --> 00:00:44.912
The program office puts
training into every gate.

14
00:00:44.912 --> 00:00:48.898
Supervisors own completion;
the help desk manager decides

15
00:00:48.898 --> 00:00:52.801
whether the desk is ready;
communications owns one sender.

16
00:00:52.801 --> 00:00:55.262
Contractors can build and deliver it all,

17
00:00:55.262 --> 00:00:58.080
but government officials
make the decisions.
